{
  "record_type": "palt_m4b_a_validation_report/1.0",
  "milestone": "PALT-M4B-A",
  "validator": "palette_moulded_validators/1.0",
  "valid": false,
  "failure_count": 1,
  "declared_count": 5,
  "findings": [
    {
      "code": "PAN_POCKET_INTERSECTION",
      "message": "the pan intersects the pocket wall by 0.0542 mm at z 2.6500 \u2014 the 0.6 mm floor fillet reaches radius 12.9458 where the pan needs 13.0",
      "severity": "FAIL",
      "interference_mm": 0.054217,
      "at_z_mm": 2.65,
      "source": "pan_seating"
    },
    {
      "code": "CONTRACT_VALUE_DIVERGENCE",
      "severity": "DECLARED",
      "source": "contract",
      "message": "pocket diameter: the owner-accepted PALT-M2/M3 layout module is 26.6 mm (26.0 pan + 2 x 0.30 tolerance) while palette_moulded_geometry.PAN_SYSTEM carries 26.8 mm (26.0 + 2 x 0.40 seating clearance). M4B-A uses 26.6 per the owner's explicit M4B-A instruction and the accepted contract; PAN_SYSTEM was NOT modified. Minimum radial pan clearance, measured at the pan base where draft makes the pocket narrowest: with a SHARP pocket corner +0.1429 mm at 26.6 and +0.2429 mm at 26.8; with the 0.6 mm moulded floor fillet this milestone actually builds, -0.0542 mm at 26.6 and +0.0458 mm at 26.8 \u2014 so the fillet, not the diameter, is what consumes the clearance. 26.6 also makes the moulded inter-pocket gap exactly the 4.0 mm the layout reserves; 26.8 would leave 3.8 mm.",
      "min_radial_clearance_mm": {
        "sharp_corner_pocket_26_6": 0.1429,
        "sharp_corner_pocket_26_8": 0.2429,
        "fillet_0_6_pocket_26_6": -0.0542,
        "fillet_0_6_pocket_26_8": 0.0458
      },
      "owner_decision_required": true
    },
    {
      "code": "UNMODELLED_CONTRACT_FEATURE",
      "severity": "DECLARED",
      "source": "contract",
      "message": "MOULDING.wall_to_floor_radius_mm (0.8) is NOT applied to the pocket. M4B-A interprets it as the base-cavity wall-to-floor radius and applies MOULDING.internal_fillet_mm (0.6) to both pocket transitions. Neither value seats the pan at 26.6: at 0.8 mm the clearance is -0.1699 mm and at 0.6 mm it is -0.0542 mm. This interpretation requires owner confirmation.",
      "clearance_at_fillet_0_8_mm": -0.1699,
      "clearance_at_fillet_0_6_mm": -0.0542,
      "owner_decision_required": true
    },
    {
      "code": "UNMODELLED_CONTRACT_FEATURE",
      "severity": "DECLARED",
      "source": "geometry",
      "message": "structural rib interfaces, hinge reinforcement interface and clasp reinforcement interface are recorded as declared interface regions, not raised geometry. The tray is currently a solid moulded block between pockets, so ribs would sit inside solid material and carry no load. Raised interfaces belong with the hinge and clasp rebuild in M4B-B.",
      "interface_regions": {
        "hinge_reinforcement_interface": {
          "edge": "TOP_EDGE",
          "y_mm": 56.0,
          "band_mm": 1.2,
          "status": "DECLARED_NOT_MODELLED"
        },
        "clasp_reinforcement_interface": {
          "edge": "BOTTOM_EDGE",
          "y_mm": -56.0,
          "band_mm": 1.0,
          "status": "DECLARED_NOT_MODELLED"
        },
        "structural_rib_interfaces": {
          "x_mm": [
            -15.3,
            15.3
          ],
          "span_y_mm": [
            -53.0,
            53.0
          ],
          "thickness_mm": 1.0,
          "status": "DECLARED_NOT_MODELLED"
        },
        "tray_footprint_mm": [
          112.0,
          112.0
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "code": "SECTION_THICKNESS_RISK",
      "severity": "DECLARED",
      "source": "moulding",
      "message": "nominal wall variation: the pocket floor is 1.0 mm while the inter-pocket land is up to 2.84 mm wide and the tray is 5.65 mm thick as a solid block. That is a section variation above 5:1, which would sink and distort in ABS. Hollowing the underside to a uniform wall is proposed for M4B-B; it changes no elevation in this contract.",
      "owner_decision_required": true
    },
    {
      "code": "PAN_POCKET_INTERSECTION",
      "severity": "DECLARED",
      "source": "solved_envelope",
      "message": "solved envelope for the pan interference. The conflict is between three contract values that were never checked together before: a 26.6 mm pocket, a 0.6 mm moulded floor fillet, and a 26.0 mm pan modelled with a SHARP bottom corner. Three independent resolutions, none applied: (a) reduce the pocket floor fillet to <= 0.5063 mm; (b) keep 0.6 mm and open the pocket to >= 26.7084 mm; (c) give the metal pan its true drawn base radius \u2014 a real drawn pan carries roughly 0.3-0.5 mm there, and a convex pan base radius nests inside the concave pocket fillet, restoring the full +0.1429 mm sharp-corner clearance. (c) is the most likely correct answer because it corrects a known simplification in the PAN model rather than changing any tray dimension, but it is a pan-supplier fact and is NOT_MANUFACTURER_CONFIRMED. No dimension was altered to make validation pass.",
      "max_floor_fillet_mm": 0.5063,
      "min_pocket_diameter_mm": 26.7084,
      "sharp_corner_clearance_mm": 0.1429,
      "measured_interference_mm": 0.0542,
      "owner_decision_required": true
    }
  ],
